{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JZ1rwTLjGzMU4VCJMgRA69","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Dashboard â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n2\t\n3\ttest-command: python -m pytest tests/ -k dashboard -q\n4\t\n5\t**North Star:** A locally-served, read-only web dashboard giving John one morning view of Aurora's\n6\tnightly fleet â€” results + health at a glance + a visual catalog explorer â€” so he never reads raw\n7\tJSON/markdown. Read-only against `kb/aurora.db` (`mode=ro`) and `reports/`; never writes the KB,\n8\tlibrary, or reports; never reads `.env`; bound to `127.0.0.1:5001`. Additive only â€” new code under\n9\t`dashboard/` + a root launcher + `tests/test_dashboard_*.py`; no edits to existing Aurora modules,\n10\tno migrations. A self-contained blueprint-factory + Flask-agnostic data layer so it can later mount\n11\tas an Anchor tab. The working tree is production â€” every wave ends clean and committed. No test\n12\tweakening; the count may only rise.\n13\t\n14\t> Stage-0 lock + gap decisions: `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/STAGE0-FRAMING.md`. Data contract\n15\t> grounded in `kb/schema.sql` and the live `reports/` surfaces (2026-06-11). Waves run in series.\n16\t> Live-KB row counts cited are 2026-06-11 snapshots and drift; every query resolves its set by rule.\n17\t\n18\t## Module shape (target, end-state)\n19\t```\n20\tdashboard/\n21\t  __init__.py            # exports create_blueprint(), create_app()\n22\t  config.py              # DashboardConfig: kb path, reports path, port â€” defaults to repo paths\n23\t  data/\n24\t    __init__.py\n25\t    db.py                # ro_connect(): read-only sqlite (file:...?mode=ro), WAL-aware; never writes\n26\t    catalog.py           # artifacts / taxonomy / taste / link_health / hh_events queries\n27\t    reports.py           # readers for reports/ (morning summary, briefing, weekly, per-sweep, backfills)\n28\t    health.py            # runs status, critic_c degrade, noise_audit, backfill audits, dead links\n29\t    freshness.py         # per-source mtime/row stamps + a combined fingerprint\n30\t  web/\n31\t    blueprint.py         # Flask Blueprint factory: /api/* routes (state, fingerprint, morning,\n32\t                         #   health, sweeps, catalog) â€” depends only on the data layer\n33\t    static/\n34\t      dashboard.html     # single-page shell\n35\t      dashboard.css\n36\t      dashboard.js       # fetch + render panels; fingerprint poll\n37\t      map.js             # taxonomy map (D3 idiom from library/_map.html)\n38\taurora_dashboard.py      # root launcher (mirror anchor_server.py): create_app().run(127.0.0.1, 5001)\n39\ttests/\n40\t  test_dashboard_data.py    # data layer: ro handle, queries, report readers, freshness (fixtures)\n41\t  test_dashboard_web.py     # route contracts + embeddability (blueprint mounts on a bare Flask app)\n42\t```\n43\tThe data layer NEVER imports Flask; the blueprint NEVER imports the orchestrator/sweep code.\n44\t\n45\t## Wave 1 â€” Read-only scaffold + data layer + serving shell\n46\t\n47\t**Intent:** Stand up the self-contained package, the proven read-only DB handle, the report-readers\n48\tskeleton, the app/blueprint factory, and a live-serving HTML shell with a freshness header and a\n49\tfingerprint poll â€” the spine every later panel hangs on. This wave fixes the architecture\n50\t(read-only safety + embeddable boundary) before any feature.\n51\t\n52\t**Deliverables:** `dashboard/` package as above (stubs for `catalog/health/reports` returning typed\n53\tempties are fine this wave, but `db.ro_connect`, `freshness`, the blueprint factory, and the shell\n54\tare real). `dashboard/data/db.py::ro_connect(kb_path)` opens\n55\t`sqlite3.connect(f\"file:{kb_path}?mode=ro\", uri=True)` with `PRAGMA query_only=ON`; a module-level\n56\tguard wraps it so any write raises. `dashboard/web/blueprint.py::create_blueprint(config)` registers:\n57\t`GET /api/health` (liveness: `{ok, kb_present, reports_present}`), `GET /api/fingerprint` (combined\n58\tmtime/row fingerprint over the KB file + key report files), `GET /api/state` (minimal: catalog\n59\tcounts by kind + the freshness map). `dashboard/__init__.py::create_app(config=None)` builds a Flask\n60\tapp, registers the blueprint, serves `dashboard.html` at `/`. Root `aurora_dashboard.py` mirrors\n61\t`anchor_server.py` (banner, opens browser, `app.run(\"127.0.0.1\", 5001)`). Shell `dashboard.html` +\n62\t`.css` + `.js`: a header strip with the global \"as of <ts>\" stamp and a panel skeleton; JS polls\n63\t`/api/fingerprint` and re-fetches on change. `tests/test_dashboard_data.py` +\n64\t`tests/test_dashboard_web.py` (fixtures built in-test).\n65\t\n66\t**Depends on:** â€”\n67\t\n68\t**done-when:** `python -m pytest tests/ -k dashboard -q` green; `create_app()` boots in-process and\n69\t`GET /api/health` returns 200 with `kb_present`/`reports_present`; the read-only handle provably\n70\trejects a write (a test attempts an INSERT and asserts it raises); the blueprint mounts on a bare\n71\t`Flask(__name__)` with NO Aurora imports (embeddability proven); `aurora_dashboard.py` imports\n72\tclean. Clean committed tree.\n73\t\n74\t- **Given** a fixture KB opened via `ro_connect`, **when** an `INSERT`/`UPDATE` is attempted, **then** sqlite raises (read-only enforced). [SUBTLE â€” the read-only-safety trap, hard constraint #1]\n75\t- **Given** a bare `Flask(__name__)` app, **when** `create_blueprint(config)` is registered on it, **then** `/api/health` works WITHOUT importing any Aurora sweep module (embeddability â€” proves the Anchor-tab boundary). [SUBTLE â€” the coupling trap, PM2]\n76\t- **Given** a missing KB or reports dir, **when** `/api/health` is hit, **then** it returns 200 with `kb_present:false`/`reports_present:false` (fails soft, never 500). \n77\t- **Given** a change to a fixture report file, **then** `/api/fingerprint` changes (poll/refresh works).\n78\t\n79\t## Wave 2 â€” The morning glance panel\n80\t\n81\t**Intent:** The first thing John sees: last night's results + spend + headline health, read straight\n82\tfrom the briefing surfaces the nightly run already wrote â€” no recomputation.\n83\t\n84\t**Deliverables:** `dashboard/data/reports.py`: `read_morning_summary()` parses\n85\t`reports/morning/latest_summary.json` (productivity_index + status + window + sample_size;\n86\t`costs.anthropic_mtd`/`gemini_mtd`; `finds`/`finds_new` by kind; `top_finds[]` name/kind/why/quality;\n87\t`noise_audit.total` + categories; `confidence_badges`; `source_quality`); `read_briefing_note()`\n88\treturns `latest_briefing_note.md` text; `read_latest_weekly()` finds the newest\n89\t`reports/weekly/<date>.md` + its date. All readers fail soft (missing file â†’ `None`/empty + a\n90\tfreshness stamp of `null`). Blueprint `GET /api/morning` composes these. Frontend \"Morning\" panel in\n91\t`dashboard.js`: top-finds cards (name Â· kind Â· why Â· star/badge quality), a productivity + adoption\n92\tline (with window + sample_size shown â€” never a bare %), a cost rollup (nightly if derivable from\n93\t`costs` rows + MTD), finds-new counts, a one-line noise headline linking to the health panel, and\n94\tthe rendered briefing note. Each block stamps \"as of <file mtime>\". Tests extend\n95\t`test_dashboard_data.py` (fixture summary.json incl. the thin-window adoption case + a\n96\tmissing-file case) + `test_dashboard_web.py` (`/api/morning` contract).\n97\t\n98\t**Depends on:** Wave 1\n99\t\n100\t**done-when:** `/api/morning` returns the parsed summary + briefing + weekly pointer from fixture\n101\treports; the panel renders top finds as named cards with why + quality, the adoption line shows\n102\twindow + sample_size, and the cost rollup shows MTD; a missing `latest_summary.json` degrades to an\n103\tempty-state card (no 500); pytest green; clean committed tree.\n104\t\n105\t- **Given** a fixture `latest_summary.json`, **when** `/api/morning` is read, **then** it returns every top_find with name/kind/why and the productivity line carries `window` + `sample_size`. \n106\t- **Given** a summary whose window is `all-time` with sample_size 21, **then** the panel shows the window label (never an unlabeled %). [SUBTLE â€” the thin-window trap inherited from the quality build]\n107\t- **Given** no `latest_summary.json`, **then** `/api/morning` returns a soft empty-state, the panel shows \"no briefing yet\", no crash.\n108\t\n109\t## Wave 3 â€” The errors / health panel (signals + in-page detail)\n110\t\n111\t**Intent:** The operator console. John sees what broke and what degraded as a first-class panel and\n112\tcan expand each signal to its underlying detail without leaving the page (G3).\n113\t\n114\t**Deliverables:** `dashboard/data/health.py` (read-only): `run_status()` reads the latest `runs` row\n115\tper sweep (status, started/finished, `critic_c_status`/`_errors` â†’ a degrade flag); `noise_audit()`\n116\treads `latest_summary.json`'s `noise_audit` block AND, for the catalog-derived categories, the\n117\toffending rows by rule from the KB (e.g. dead `library` links, retired-in-surface) so each non-zero\n118\tcategory can expand to examples; `backfill_audits()` scans `reports/backfills/*.json` for the latest\n119\tper-kind audit and flags any with non-empty error/changed sets; `recent_rejects()` tails the newest\n120\t`reports/screen_rejects/<date>.jsonl` (sample N); `sweep_log_tail(kind, n)` returns the last N lines\n121\tof the relevant sweep log if present (path-allowlisted to `reports/` â€” never an arbitrary path).\n122\tBlueprint `GET /api/health` (extend W1 liveness into the full health object) + `GET\n123\t/api/health/detail?signal=<id>` returning the expandable detail for one signal. Frontend \"Health\"\n124\tpanel: a row per signal with a status pill (ok/degraded/error) and a count; each row expands inline\n125\tto render the detail (log tail / audit JSON / offending rows / reject samples). Degrade and non-zero\n126\tnoise are visually loud. Tests: fixture KB with a degraded run + non-zero noise + a failing backfill\n127\taudit; assert the panel object flags each and the detail endpoint returns the rows; path-allowlist\n128\ttest (a `..`/absolute path to `sweep_log_tail` is refused).\n129\t\n130\t**Depends on:** Wave 2\n131\t\n132\t**done-when:** `/api/health` returns per-sweep run status + degrade flags + noise categories +\n133\tbackfill-audit pass/fail + dead-link count; `/api/health/detail` expands each non-zero signal to its\n134\tunderlying rows/log/JSON in-page; a `..`/absolute path is refused by the log-tail allowlist; an\n135\tall-green fixture shows all-ok with nothing loud; pytest green; clean committed tree.\n136\t\n137\t- **Given** a fixture run with `critic_c_status='degraded'`, **then** `/api/health` flags that sweep degraded and the detail endpoint returns the reason. \n138\t- **Given** `noise_audit.dead_library_links > 0`, **then** the signal is non-zero AND its detail expands to the offending library paths. [G3 â€” signals + in-page detail]\n139\t- **Given** a backfill audit JSON with a non-empty error set, **then** the panel flags it and the detail renders that JSON. \n140\t- **Given** `signal` resolving to a path outside `reports/` (e.g. `../../.env` or an absolute path), **then** `sweep_log_tail`/detail refuses it. [SUBTLE â€” the path-traversal / secret-exposure trap, hard constraint #2]\n141\t\n142\t## Wave 4 â€” \"What was new\" per-sweep results browser\n143\t\n144\t**Intent:** Drill from \"0/2/8 new last night\" into the actual per-sweep results the run wrote.\n145\t\n146\t**Deliverables:** `dashboard/data/reports.py` gains `list_sweep_dates(kind)` (dirs under\n147\t`reports/<kind>/`, newest first) and `read_sweep(kind, date)` (renders the report files in that\n148\tdate dir â€” md/json â€” with the file's stamp; path-allowlisted to `reports/<kind>/`). Blueprint `GET\n149\t/api/sweeps` (available kinds + recent dates) + `GET /api/sweep/<kind>/<date>`. Frontend \"What was\n150\tnew\" panel: a kindÃ—date selector (defaults to the latest date) rendering that sweep's report; links\n151\tfrom the morning panel's finds-new counts jump here. Tests: fixture per-sweep dirs; date listing\n152\torder; `read_sweep` rejects a traversal date/kind; missing date â†’ soft empty.\n153\t\n154\t**Depends on:** Wave 3\n155\t\n156\t**done-when:** `/api/sweeps` lists the kinds + dates present under fixture `reports/`; `/api/sweep/\n157\t<kind>/<date>` returns that date's rendered report; a `..` kind/date is refused; the panel defaults\n158\tto the latest date and the morning finds-new links reach it; pytest green; clean committed tree.\n159\t\n160\t- **Given** fixture `reports/agents/2026-06-10/` and `/2026-06-11/`, **then** `list_sweep_dates('agents')` returns both newest-first and `/api/sweep/agents/2026-06-11` renders that dir.\n161\t- **Given** a `kind`/`date` containing `..` or an absolute path, **then** the reader refuses it (allowlist to `reports/<kind>/`). [SUBTLE â€” path-traversal trap]\n162\t- **Given** a date dir that does not exist, **then** the endpoint returns a soft empty-state (no 500).\n163\t\n164\t## Wave 5 â€” The catalog taxonomy map\n165\t\n166\t**Intent:** The catalog explorer (G1 v1): a hierarchical map of the live catalog John can see and\n167\tclick, doubling as a health instrument (taste distribution, dead-link/star overlays).\n168\t\n169\t**Deliverables:** `dashboard/data/catalog.py` (read-only): `taxonomy_map()` queries non-retired\n170\t`artifacts` LEFT JOIN `embeddings` (on artifact_id) grouped by `kind Ã— embeddings.domain_path`\n171\t(NULL domain_path â†’ an \"unclassified\" bucket), aggregating count, mean `interest_score`, and a\n172\tdead-link/stars overlay from `link_health` (latest probe per artifact: `gh_stargazers`,\n173\t`http_status`/`stale_url` â†’ dead flag); `artifacts_in(kind, domain_path)` returns the artifact list\n174\tfor a wedge (name, slug, interest_score, interest_why, stars, dead-flag, canonical_url, usage count\n175\tfrom `hh_events`). Blueprint `GET /api/catalog/map` + `GET /api/catalog/artifacts?kind=&domain=`.\n176\tFrontend `map.js` reusing the `library/_map.html` D3 idiom: a sunburst/icicle of kindâ†’domain_path,\n177\tcolor = mean taste, size = count, a dead-link/stars overlay; click a wedge â†’ the filtered artifact\n178\tlist (name Â· taste why Â· stars Â· usage Â· dead-flag Â· link). \"as of\" stamp from the KB mtime. Tests:\n179\tfixture artifacts+embeddings+link_health+hh_events; assert the map groups + aggregates correctly,\n180\tthe unclassified bucket catches NULL domain_path, retired rows are excluded, and `artifacts_in`\n181\treturns the wedge rows.\n182\t\n183\t**Depends on:** Wave 4\n184\t\n185\t**done-when:** `/api/catalog/map` returns kindÃ—domain_path groups with count + mean taste + overlay;\n186\t`/api/catalog/artifacts` returns a wedge's artifacts with taste why + stars + usage; retired rows\n187\tare excluded; NULL domain_path lands in \"unclassified\"; the map renders and click-to-filter works;\n188\tpytest green; clean committed tree.\n189\t\n190\t- **Given** fixture artifacts across kinds/domains with some retired and some NULL domain_path, **then** `taxonomy_map()` excludes retired rows and buckets NULLs as \"unclassified\" with correct counts + mean taste.\n191\t- **Given** a wedge (kind, domain_path), **then** `artifacts_in` returns exactly that wedge's non-retired artifacts with interest_why, stars, and hh usage. \n192\t- **Given** an artifact with a dead `link_health` probe, **then** the map overlay marks its wedge and the artifact row carries a dead-flag. \n193\t\n194\t## Wave 6 â€” Polish, embeddability proof, docs (+ deferred-graph note)\n195\t\n196\t**Intent:** Make it operator-grade and prove the Anchor-tab boundary; close the trio honestly.\n197\t\n198\t**Deliverables:** global \"as of\" header aggregating per-panel freshness; empty/error states audited\n199\tacross panels; `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/DASHBOARD.md` (run instructions mirroring Anchor's,\n200\tthe module map, and the **exact steps to mount as an Anchor tab** â€” register the blueprint, drop the\n201\tpanel into Anchor's shell); an embeddability integration test that mounts `create_blueprint` on a\n202\tsecond bare Flask app and exercises every `/api/*` route; a brief **deferred-work** section naming\n203\tthe force-directed knowledge-graph (data sources: shared `domain_path`, `github_network_parent`\n204\tlineage, `prov_edges`, `hh_events`) as the next wave, not built. Final local smoke: boot\n205\t`aurora_dashboard.py` against the live read-only KB, confirm every panel renders, confirm zero writes\n206\tto `kb/aurora.db`/`reports/` (mtimes unchanged).\n207\t\n208\t**Depends on:** Wave 5\n209\t\n210\t**done-when:** `DASHBOARD.md` documents run + Anchor-mount steps; the embeddability test mounts the\n211\tblueprint on a bare app and all routes pass; a live read-only smoke shows every panel rendering with\n212\tKB/reports mtimes unchanged after a session; the deferred-graph note is recorded; pytest green; clean\n213\tcommitted tree.\n214\t\n215\t- **Given** the blueprint mounted on a second bare Flask app, **then** every `/api/*` route responds (full embeddability, not just `/api/health`). [SUBTLE â€” the Anchor-tab boundary, PM2]\n216\t- **Given** a live read-only smoke session, **then** `kb/aurora.db` and `reports/` file mtimes are unchanged afterward (no writes). [SUBTLE â€” read-only guarantee, hard constraint #1]\n217\t- **Given** `DASHBOARD.md`, **then** it states the run command, the module boundary, and the exact Anchor-tab mount steps.\n218\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7460d624-e407-40b0-9c08-72e772205b44","uuid":"b3224400-e824-49a5-9c84-99e831ff2a90","timestamp":"2026-06-17T21:05:04.867Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\foreman-handoff-dashboard\\IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md","content":"# Aurora Dashboard â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n\ntest-command: python -m pytest tests/ -k dashboard -q\n\n**North Star:** A locally-served, read-only web dashboard giving John one morning view of Aurora's\nnightly fleet â€” results + health at a glance + a visual catalog explorer â€” so he never reads raw\nJSON/markdown. Read-only against `kb/aurora.db` (`mode=ro`) and `reports/`; never writes the KB,\nlibrary, or reports; never reads `.env`; bound to `127.0.0.1:5001`. Additive only â€” new code under\n`dashboard/` + a root launcher + `tests/test_dashboard_*.py`; no edits to existing Aurora modules,\nno migrations. A self-contained blueprint-factory + Flask-agnostic data layer so it can later mount\nas an Anchor tab. The working tree is production â€” every wave ends clean and committed. No test\nweakening; the count may only rise.\n\n> Stage-0 lock + gap decisions: `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/STAGE0-FRAMING.md`. Data contract\n> grounded in `kb/schema.sql` and the live `reports/` surfaces (2026-06-11). Waves run in series.\n> Live-KB row counts cited are 2026-06-11 snapshots and drift; every query resolves its set by rule.\n\n## Module shape (target, end-state)\n```\ndashboard/\n  __init__.py            # exports create_blueprint(), create_app()\n  config.py              # DashboardConfig: kb path, reports path, port â€” defaults to repo paths\n  data/\n    __init__.py\n    db.py                # ro_connect(): read-only sqlite (file:...?mode=ro), WAL-aware; never writes\n    catalog.py           # artifacts / taxonomy / taste / link_health / hh_events queries\n    reports.py           # readers for reports/ (morning summary, briefing, weekly, per-sweep, backfills)\n    health.py            # runs status, critic_c degrade, noise_audit, backfill audits, dead links\n    freshness.py         # per-source mtime/row stamps + a combined fingerprint\n  web/\n    blueprint.py         # Flask Blueprint factory: /api/* routes (state, fingerprint, morning,\n                         #   health, sweeps, catalog) â€” depends only on the data layer\n    static/\n      dashboard.html     # single-page shell\n      dashboard.css\n      dashboard.js       # fetch + render panels; fingerprint poll\n      map.js             # taxonomy map (D3 idiom from library/_map.html)\naurora_dashboard.py      # root launcher (mirror anchor_server.py): create_app().run(127.0.0.1, 5001)\ntests/\n  test_dashboard_data.py    # data layer: ro handle, queries, report readers, freshness (fixtures)\n  test_dashboard_web.py     # route contracts + embeddability (blueprint mounts on a bare Flask app)\n```\nThe data layer NEVER imports Flask; the blueprint NEVER imports the orchestrator/sweep code.\n\n## Wave 1 â€” Read-only scaffold + data layer + serving shell\n\n**Intent:** Stand up the self-contained package, the proven read-only DB handle, the report-readers\nskeleton, the app/blueprint factory, and a live-serving HTML shell with a freshness header and a\nfingerprint poll â€” the spine every later panel hangs on. This wave fixes the architecture\n(read-only safety + embeddable boundary) before any feature.\n\n**Deliverables:** `dashboard/` package as above (stubs for `catalog/health/reports` returning typed\nempties are fine this wave, but `db.ro_connect`, `freshness`, the blueprint factory, and the shell\nare real). `dashboard/data/db.py::ro_connect(kb_path)` opens\n`sqlite3.connect(f\"file:{kb_path}?mode=ro\", uri=True)` with `PRAGMA query_only=ON`; a module-level\nguard wraps it so any write raises. `dashboard/web/blueprint.py::create_blueprint(config)` registers:\n`GET /api/health` (liveness: `{ok, kb_present, reports_present}`), `GET /api/fingerprint` (combined\nmtime/row fingerprint over the KB file + key report files), `GET /api/state` (minimal: catalog\ncounts by kind + the freshness map). `dashboard/__init__.py::create_app(config=None)` builds a Flask\napp, registers the blueprint, serves `dashboard.html` at `/`. Root `aurora_dashboard.py` mirrors\n`anchor_server.py` (banner, opens browser, `app.run(\"127.0.0.1\", 5001)`). Shell `dashboard.html` +\n`.css` + `.js`: a header strip with the global \"as of <ts>\" stamp and a panel skeleton; JS polls\n`/api/fingerprint` and re-fetches on change. `tests/test_dashboard_data.py` +\n`tests/test_dashboard_web.py` (fixtures built in-test).\n\n**Depends on:** â€”\n\n**done-when:** `python -m pytest tests/ -k dashboard -q` green; `create_app()` boots in-process and\n`GET /api/health` returns 200 with `kb_present`/`reports_present`; the read-only handle provably\nrejects a write (a test attempts an INSERT and asserts it raises); the blueprint mounts on a bare\n`Flask(__name__)` with NO Aurora imports (embeddability proven); `aurora_dashboard.py` imports\nclean. Clean committed tree.\n\n- **Given** a fixture KB opened via `ro_connect`, **when** an `INSERT`/`UPDATE` is attempted, **then** sqlite raises (read-only enforced). [SUBTLE â€” the read-only-safety trap, hard constraint #1]\n- **Given** a bare `Flask(__name__)` app, **when** `create_blueprint(config)` is registered on it, **then** `/api/health` works WITHOUT importing any Aurora sweep module (embeddability â€” proves the Anchor-tab boundary). [SUBTLE â€” the coupling trap, PM2]\n- **Given** a missing KB or reports dir, **when** `/api/health` is hit, **then** it returns 200 with `kb_present:false`/`reports_present:false` (fails soft, never 500). \n- **Given** a change to a fixture report file, **then** `/api/fingerprint` changes (poll/refresh works).\n\n## Wave 2 â€” The morning glance panel\n\n**Intent:** The first thing John sees: last night's results + spend + headline health, read straight\nfrom the briefing surfaces the nightly run already wrote â€” no recomputation.\n\n**Deliverables:** `dashboard/data/reports.py`: `read_morning_summary()` parses\n`reports/morning/latest_summary.json` (productivity_index + status + window + sample_size;\n`costs.anthropic_mtd`/`gemini_mtd`; `finds`/`finds_new` by kind; `top_finds[]` name/kind/why/quality;\n`noise_audit.total` + categories; `confidence_badges`; `source_quality`); `read_briefing_note()`\nreturns `latest_briefing_note.md` text; `read_latest_weekly()` finds the newest\n`reports/weekly/<date>.md` + its date. All readers fail soft (missing file â†’ `None`/empty + a\nfreshness stamp of `null`). Blueprint `GET /api/morning` composes these. Frontend \"Morning\" panel in\n`dashboard.js`: top-finds cards (name Â· kind Â· why Â· star/badge quality), a productivity + adoption\nline (with window + sample_size shown â€” never a bare %), a cost rollup (nightly if derivable from\n`costs` rows + MTD), finds-new counts, a one-line noise headline linking to the health panel, and\nthe rendered briefing note. Each block stamps \"as of <file mtime>\". Tests extend\n`test_dashboard_data.py` (fixture summary.json incl. the thin-window adoption case + a\nmissing-file case) + `test_dashboard_web.py` (`/api/morning` contract).\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 1\n\n**done-when:** `/api/morning` returns the parsed summary + briefing + weekly pointer from fixture\nreports; the panel renders top finds as named cards with why + quality, the adoption line shows\nwindow + sample_size, and the cost rollup shows MTD; a missing `latest_summary.json` degrades to an\nempty-state card (no 500); pytest green; clean committed tree.\n\n- **Given** a fixture `latest_summary.json`, **when** `/api/morning` is read, **then** it returns every top_find with name/kind/why and the productivity line carries `window` + `sample_size`. \n- **Given** a summary whose window is `all-time` with sample_size 21, **then** the panel shows the window label (never an unlabeled %). [SUBTLE â€” the thin-window trap inherited from the quality build]\n- **Given** no `latest_summary.json`, **then** `/api/morning` returns a soft empty-state, the panel shows \"no briefing yet\", no crash.\n\n## Wave 3 â€” The errors / health panel (signals + in-page detail)\n\n**Intent:** The operator console. John sees what broke and what degraded as a first-class panel and\ncan expand each signal to its underlying detail without leaving the page (G3).\n\n**Deliverables:** `dashboard/data/health.py` (read-only): `run_status()` reads the latest `runs` row\nper sweep (status, started/finished, `critic_c_status`/`_errors` â†’ a degrade flag); `noise_audit()`\nreads `latest_summary.json`'s `noise_audit` block AND, for the catalog-derived categories, the\noffending rows by rule from the KB (e.g. dead `library` links, retired-in-surface) so each non-zero\ncategory can expand to examples; `backfill_audits()` scans `reports/backfills/*.json` for the latest\nper-kind audit and flags any with non-empty error/changed sets; `recent_rejects()` tails the newest\n`reports/screen_rejects/<date>.jsonl` (sample N); `sweep_log_tail(kind, n)` returns the last N lines\nof the relevant sweep log if present (path-allowlisted to `reports/` â€” never an arbitrary path).\nBlueprint `GET /api/health` (extend W1 liveness into the full health object) + `GET\n/api/health/detail?signal=<id>` returning the expandable detail for one signal. Frontend \"Health\"\npanel: a row per signal with a status pill (ok/degraded/error) and a count; each row expands inline\nto render the detail (log tail / audit JSON / offending rows / reject samples). Degrade and non-zero\nnoise are visually loud. Tests: fixture KB with a degraded run + non-zero noise + a failing backfill\naudit; assert the panel object flags each and the detail endpoint returns the rows; path-allowlist\ntest (a `..`/absolute path to `sweep_log_tail` is refused).\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 2\n\n**done-when:** `/api/health` returns per-sweep run status + degrade flags + noise categories +\nbackfill-audit pass/fail + dead-link count; `/api/health/detail` expands each non-zero signal to its\nunderlying rows/log/JSON in-page; a `..`/absolute path is refused by the log-tail allowlist; an\nall-green fixture shows all-ok with nothing loud; pytest green; clean committed tree.\n\n- **Given** a fixture run with `critic_c_status='degraded'`, **then** `/api/health` flags that sweep degraded and the detail endpoint returns the reason. \n- **Given** `noise_audit.dead_library_links > 0`, **then** the signal is non-zero AND its detail expands to the offending library paths. [G3 â€” signals + in-page detail]\n- **Given** a backfill audit JSON with a non-empty error set, **then** the panel flags it and the detail renders that JSON. \n- **Given** `signal` resolving to a path outside `reports/` (e.g. `../../.env` or an absolute path), **then** `sweep_log_tail`/detail refuses it. [SUBTLE â€” the path-traversal / secret-exposure trap, hard constraint #2]\n\n## Wave 4 â€” \"What was new\" per-sweep results browser\n\n**Intent:** Drill from \"0/2/8 new last night\" into the actual per-sweep results the run wrote.\n\n**Deliverables:** `dashboard/data/reports.py` gains `list_sweep_dates(kind)` (dirs under\n`reports/<kind>/`, newest first) and `read_sweep(kind, date)` (renders the report files in that\ndate dir â€” md/json â€” with the file's stamp; path-allowlisted to `reports/<kind>/`). Blueprint `GET\n/api/sweeps` (available kinds + recent dates) + `GET /api/sweep/<kind>/<date>`. Frontend \"What was\nnew\" panel: a kindÃ—date selector (defaults to the latest date) rendering that sweep's report; links\nfrom the morning panel's finds-new counts jump here. Tests: fixture per-sweep dirs; date listing\norder; `read_sweep` rejects a traversal date/kind; missing date â†’ soft empty.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 3\n\n**done-when:** `/api/sweeps` lists the kinds + dates present under fixture `reports/`; `/api/sweep/\n<kind>/<date>` returns that date's rendered report; a `..` kind/date is refused; the panel defaults\nto the latest date and the morning finds-new links reach it; pytest green; clean committed tree.\n\n- **Given** fixture `reports/agents/2026-06-10/` and `/2026-06-11/`, **then** `list_sweep_dates('agents')` returns both newest-first and `/api/sweep/agents/2026-06-11` renders that dir.\n- **Given** a `kind`/`date` containing `..` or an absolute path, **then** the reader refuses it (allowlist to `reports/<kind>/`). [SUBTLE â€” path-traversal trap]\n- **Given** a date dir that does not exist, **then** the endpoint returns a soft empty-state (no 500).\n\n## Wave 5 â€” The catalog taxonomy map\n\n**Intent:** The catalog explorer (G1 v1): a hierarchical map of the live catalog John can see and\nclick, doubling as a health instrument (taste distribution, dead-link/star overlays).\n\n**Deliverables:** `dashboard/data/catalog.py` (read-only): `taxonomy_map()` queries non-retired\n`artifacts` LEFT JOIN `embeddings` (on artifact_id) grouped by `kind Ã— embeddings.domain_path`\n(NULL domain_path â†’ an \"unclassified\" bucket), aggregating count, mean `interest_score`, and a\ndead-link/stars overlay from `link_health` (latest probe per artifact: `gh_stargazers`,\n`http_status`/`stale_url` â†’ dead flag); `artifacts_in(kind, domain_path)` returns the artifact list\nfor a wedge (name, slug, interest_score, interest_why, stars, dead-flag, canonical_url, usage count\nfrom `hh_events`). Blueprint `GET /api/catalog/map` + `GET /api/catalog/artifacts?kind=&domain=`.\nFrontend `map.js` reusing the `library/_map.html` D3 idiom: a sunburst/icicle of kindâ†’domain_path,\ncolor = mean taste, size = count, a dead-link/stars overlay; click a wedge â†’ the filtered artifact\nlist (name Â· taste why Â· stars Â· usage Â· dead-flag Â· link). \"as of\" stamp from the KB mtime. Tests:\nfixture artifacts+embeddings+link_health+hh_events; assert the map groups + aggregates correctly,\nthe unclassified bucket catches NULL domain_path, retired rows are excluded, and `artifacts_in`\nreturns the wedge rows.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 4\n\n**done-when:** `/api/catalog/map` returns kindÃ—domain_path groups with count + mean taste + overlay;\n`/api/catalog/artifacts` returns a wedge's artifacts with taste why + stars + usage; retired rows\nare excluded; NULL domain_path lands in \"unclassified\"; the map renders and click-to-filter works;\npytest green; clean committed tree.\n\n- **Given** fixture artifacts across kinds/domains with some retired and some NULL domain_path, **then** `taxonomy_map()` excludes retired rows and buckets NULLs as \"unclassified\" with correct counts + mean taste.\n- **Given** a wedge (kind, domain_path), **then** `artifacts_in` returns exactly that wedge's non-retired artifacts with interest_why, stars, and hh usage. \n- **Given** an artifact with a dead `link_health` probe, **then** the map overlay marks its wedge and the artifact row carries a dead-flag. \n\n## Wave 6 â€” Polish, embeddability proof, docs (+ deferred-graph note)\n\n**Intent:** Make it operator-grade and prove the Anchor-tab boundary; close the trio honestly.\n\n**Deliverables:** global \"as of\" header aggregating per-panel freshness; empty/error states audited\nacross panels; `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/DASHBOARD.md` (run instructions mirroring Anchor's,\nthe module map, and the **exact steps to mount as an Anchor tab** â€” register the blueprint, drop the\npanel into Anchor's shell); an embeddability integration test that mounts `create_blueprint` on a\nsecond bare Flask app and exercises every `/api/*` route; a brief **deferred-work** section naming\nthe force-directed knowledge-graph (data sources: shared `domain_path`, `github_network_parent`\nlineage, `prov_edges`, `hh_events`) as the next wave, not built. Final local smoke: boot\n`aurora_dashboard.py` against the live read-only KB, confirm every panel renders, confirm zero writes\nto `kb/aurora.db`/`reports/` (mtimes unchanged).\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 5\n\n**done-when:** `DASHBOARD.md` documents run + Anchor-mount steps; the embeddability test mounts the\nblueprint on a bare app and all routes pass; a live read-only smoke shows every panel rendering with\nKB/reports mtimes unchanged after a session; the deferred-graph note is recorded; pytest green; clean\ncommitted tree.\n\n- **Given** the blueprint mounted on a second bare Flask app, **then** every `/api/*` route responds (full embeddability, not just `/api/health`). [SUBTLE â€” the Anchor-tab boundary, PM2]\n- **Given** a live read-only smoke session, **then** `kb/aurora.db` and `reports/` file mtimes are unchanged afterward (no writes). [SUBTLE â€” read-only guarantee, hard constraint #1]\n- **Given** `DASHBOARD.md`, **then** it states the run command, the module boundary, and the exact Anchor-tab mount steps.\n","numLines":218,"startLine":1,"totalLines":218}}}
